          "thinking": "Now I understand the codebase. Let me analyze what needs to be done:\n\n1. Add a `--max-pending-hours H` option to the `check-anchors` command\n2. When this option is provided, check if any range head's proof is still pending and its Sigstore attestation time is more than H hours ago\n3. If so, exit 1 and print a message containing `still pending N h` where N is the whole number of hours since the attestation\n4. Without the option, behavior is unchanged (pending proofs are accepted, exit 0)\n5. All existing tests must still pass\n\nLooking at the `cmd_check_anchors` function, I can see:\n- It loads the chain and checks anchors\n- For each sigstore anchor, it gets the integrated time `t` from the bundle\n- For each ots anchor, it calls `check_ots` which returns the earliest Bitcoin block time or `None` if pending\n- The `stamped` set tracks which sequences have .ots files\n- The `ranges` list contains tuples of (from_seq, to_seq, commit) for each sigstore anchor\n\nThe logic I need to add:\n- For each range head (which is the `to_seq` in ranges), check if its .ots proof is pending (i.e., `check_ots` returned `None`)\n- If pending, get the sigstore attestation time for that range head\n- Calculate hours since attestation\n- If hours > H, print error and exit 1\n\nLet me trace through the code more carefully:\n\nIn `cmd_check_anchors`:\n- `rows` collects anchor info including `existed_by` which is `iso(t)` or \"pending\"\n- `ranges` collects (from_seq, to_seq, commit) for sigstore anchors\n- `stamped` tracks which seqs have .ots files\n- After processing all anchors, it checks that every range head (hi) is in stamped\n\nThe `check_ots` function returns `None` if the proof is still pending (no Bitcoin block attestations).\n\nI need to:\n1. Add the `--max-pending-hours` argument to the check-anchors parser\n2. In `cmd_check_anchors`, when this option is provided, track for each range head:\n   - The sigstore attestation time (integrated_time)\n   - Whether the .ots proof is pending\n3. After all checks, for any pending range head, calculate hours since attestation\n4. If > H hours, add to bad list with the required message format\n\nLet me look at how the sigstore attestation time is associated with each range. Currently, `ranges` only stores (from_seq, to_seq, commit). I need to also store the integrated_time for each range.\n\nLet me modify the code.",
