          "type": "thinking",
          "thinking": "All tests pass. Now let me verify the new functionality works correctly by testing it manually. I need to test:\n1. Without --max-pending-hours, pending proofs are accepted (exit 0)\n2. With --max-pending-hours, if a pending proof's attestation is older than H hours, exit 1 with \"still pending N h\" message\n3. With --max-pending-hours, if a pending proof's attestation is younger than H hours, exit 0\n\nLet me create a simple test to verify this works. But first, I should check if the `check_ots` function is being called correctly. The test `test_a_missing_ots_proof_for_a_range_head_is_caught` stubs `check_ots` to return `None` (which means pending). Let me verify that the logic works correctly with the stub.\n\nWait, I notice a potential issue. In the test `test_a_missing_ots_proof_for_a_range_head_is_caught`, the test stubs `check_ots` to return `None` (pending). But with my new code, when `--max-pending-hours` is not provided, it should still pass (exit 0 when the .ots file exists). Let me check if the test would still pass.\n\nActually, looking at the test more carefully:\n- It creates a stub sigstore.json and then checks that check-anchors fails because the .ots is missing\n- Then it creates a stub .ots file and checks that check-anchors passes\n- The test stubs `check_sigstore` and `check_ots` functions\n\nThe stub for `check_ots` returns `None` (pending). But the test doesn't use `--max-pending-hours`, so it should still pass. Let me verify this is working correctly.\n\nActually, wait - the test creates a stub .ots file with `open(os.path.join(self.d, \"anchors\", \"000002.ots\"), \"wb\").write(b\"stub\")` - but this is a malformed OTS file. The stub `check_ots` function just returns `None`, so it doesn't matter what the file contains.\n\nBut in my new code, I call `check_ots` again for the pending check. Since the test stubs `check_ots` to return `None`, and the test doesn't use `--max-pending-hours`, it should be fine.\n\nLet me verify by running the test again and also testing the new functionality manually.",
