        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "All 21 tests pass. The implementation is complete. Here's a summary of the changes:\n\n## Summary\n\nI added the `--max-pending-hours H` option to the `check-anchors` command in `/workspace/record/record.py`.\n\n### Changes Made:\n\n1. **Added command-line argument** (line 632-634):\n   ```python\n   p.add_argument(\"--max-pending-hours\", type=int, metavar=\"H\",\n                  help=\"exit 1 if any range head's OTS proof is still pending and its Sigstore attestation is over H hours old\")\n   ```\n\n2. **Modified `cmd_check_anchors` function** to:\n   - Track the Sigstore attestation time (`t`) for each range head by storing it in the `ranges` tuple as `(from_seq, to_seq, commit, t)`\n   - When `--max-pending-hours` is provided, check each range head's OTS proof:\n     - If the proof is still pending (`check_ots` returns `None`)\n     - Calculate whole hours since attestation: `int((now - t) // 3600)`\n     - If hours exceed `H`, add a `BAD` error with message: `anchors/NNNNNN.ots: still pending N h (attested ...)`\n   - Exit 1 if any such errors exist\n\n### Behavior:\n- **Without `--max-pending-hours`**: Unchanged - pending proofs are accepted (exit 0)\n- **With `--max-pending-hours H`**: \n  - Pending proof with attestation > H hours ago → exit 1, prints `still pending N h` to stderr\n  - Pending proof with attestation ≤ H hours ago → exit 0\n  - Confirmed proof (not pending) → always exit 0 regardless of attestation age\n\n### Testing:\n- All 21 existing tests pass\n- Manually verified the new functionality with various scenarios:\n  - No option → pending accepted\n  - Option with H < hours pending → exit 1 with correct message\n  - Option with H ≥ hours pending → exit 0\n  - Confirmed OTS proof → always exit 0\n  - Multiple range heads with different pending statuses → correctly reports only those exceeding threshold"
        }
      ],
